# A turn somebody cuts short at the pane. The vendor is working when the key
# arrives, and Escape is the whole of what ends the turn: nothing else moves
# this scenario on.
#
# The mode footer claude keeps up while it works is left off the working
# screen here, so the footer appearing is the key having arrived and nothing
# else. What a screen with one on it either way costs a reader is the idle
# rule's business, and `tests/e2e_reader.rs` is where that is asked.
hook SessionStart {"source": "startup"}
hook UserPromptSubmit {"prompt": "port the importer"}
print I'll port the importer.
await Escape
# The turn ended where it stood, and claude is back at its prompt with the
# conversation behind it. No Stop: the hooks are written around turns that run
# to their end, and this one did not.
print ❯
print   Opus 5 (1M context) │ ◈ 2% │ mock-claude (amx/port-importer-c3d) │ ◖ xhigh
print   ⏵⏵ auto mode on (shift+tab to cycle) · ← for agents
sleep 600000
